00:33:44.880 --> 00:33:48.120
They were intolerable to work with. Yes. And

00:33:48.120 --> 00:33:49.800
you know what? I'll tell you a story just to

00:33:49.800 --> 00:33:51.480
give you an idea. I'll tell you two stories.

00:33:52.920 --> 00:33:58.000
My very first briefing when I was a brand spanking

00:33:58.000 --> 00:34:04.080
new CIA officer, 35 years ago, January,

00:34:05.520 --> 00:34:10.080
was for the local Mossad and Shin Bet

00:34:10.080 --> 00:34:15.600
representatives. The briefing was on Iraq, and

00:34:15.600 --> 00:34:20.880
it included all of the Iraq analysts in the

00:34:20.880 --> 00:34:25.160
building, CIA headquarters. We do not brief the

00:34:25.160 --> 00:34:27.360
Israelis at CIA headquarters. The Israelis are

00:34:27.360 --> 00:34:30.480
not permitted in the building because when they

00:34:30.480 --> 00:34:32.400
were permitted in the building, every time they

00:34:32.400 --> 00:34:35.040
come, they would give us a gift that invariably

00:34:35.040 --> 00:34:38.720
had a bug inside of it and packed with

00:34:38.720 --> 00:34:40.600
batteries. And we're like, all right, you guys

00:34:40.600 --> 00:34:43.880
can't come here anymore. So we meet, we

00:34:43.880 --> 00:34:46.720
meet the Israelis at this offsite location in

00:34:46.720 --> 00:34:50.560
northern Virginia. And because I was the

00:34:50.560 --> 00:34:54.200
junior most analyst, I went last. So we went

00:34:54.200 --> 00:34:57.080
around the conference room table. It was about

00:34:57.080 --> 00:35:00.200
like eight or 10 of us, eight of us, I guess it

00:35:00.200 --> 00:35:02.880
was, from the most senior analysts to me, the

00:35:02.880 --> 00:35:06.320
most junior. And when they got to me, I used

00:35:06.320 --> 00:35:09.400
my real name because I was not undercover. So I

00:35:09.400 --> 00:35:11.400
said, my name is John Kiriakou, and I'm going

00:35:11.400 --> 00:35:13.400
to brief you today on Saddam Hussein and

00:35:13.400 --> 00:35:17.440
the Iraqi cabinet. And the Shin Bet guy says,

00:35:17.680 --> 00:35:21.240
please spell your name. So I spelled it. And

00:35:21.240 --> 00:35:23.040
then he looks up at me over his glasses and he

00:35:23.040 --> 00:35:29.560
goes, you are Jewish. And I said, I am not

00:35:29.560 --> 00:35:34.040
recruitable. Don't even think about it. He

00:35:34.040 --> 00:35:35.520
asked me in front of all my colleagues, I'm

00:35:35.520 --> 00:35:37.640
my Jewish, so he can target me for

00:35:37.640 --> 00:35:41.240
recruitment. Number one, number two, several

00:35:41.240 --> 00:35:48.640
years later, I transferred into a state

00:35:48.640 --> 00:35:51.800
department position. It was an honest to God

00:35:51.800 --> 00:35:53.880
state department rotation. I became the

00:35:54.200 --> 00:35:56.520
the economic officer at the American Embassy in

00:35:56.520 --> 00:36:00.640
Manama Bahrain. But there was a married couple

00:36:00.640 --> 00:36:03.400
in my office and they went, the wife went

00:36:03.400 --> 00:36:05.920
into the same position at the American

00:36:05.920 --> 00:36:09.060
Embassy in, well, it was the American

00:36:09.060 --> 00:36:13.140
consulate then in Jerusalem. So her husband,

00:36:14.020 --> 00:36:16.900
because she was the lead, her husband went

00:36:16.900 --> 00:36:20.300
to the University of Tel Aviv to learn

00:36:20.300 --> 00:36:23.420
Arabic. Because they were declared like I

00:36:23.420 --> 00:36:26.740
was to the Israelis, you know, the station

00:36:26.740 --> 00:36:28.460
chief would say, these are my two

00:36:28.460 --> 00:36:31.380
officers, you know them, they're CIA.

00:36:31.940 --> 00:36:33.940
The wife is on rotation to the state

00:36:33.940 --> 00:36:37.340
department. The husband is going to just

00:36:37.340 --> 00:36:39.620
study at the university. So they're not

00:36:39.620 --> 00:36:42.860
here for anything untoward. Well, they were

00:36:42.860 --> 00:36:45.660
invited to a party one night and at the

00:36:45.660 --> 00:36:47.420
ambassador's residence. And then when they

00:36:47.420 --> 00:36:49.980
got back to Jerusalem, they walked in the

00:36:49.980 --> 00:36:52.500
house and saw that all of their living

00:36:52.500 --> 00:36:55.540
room furniture had been rearranged. Just

00:36:55.540 --> 00:36:58.700
a message from Mossad, we can come in here

00:36:58.700 --> 00:37:01.460
anytime we want and we can do whatever we

00:37:01.460 --> 00:37:02.900
want. And there's nothing you can do

00:37:02.900 --> 00:37:09.990
about it. At Christmas time, they went to a

00:37:09.990 --> 00:37:12.790
party at the ambassador's residence. And

00:37:12.790 --> 00:37:15.790
when they got home, people had taken

00:37:15.790 --> 00:37:18.550
shits in all their toilets, right? They

00:37:18.550 --> 00:37:21.790
have three bedrooms, three bathroom

00:37:21.790 --> 00:37:24.990
house, and people had taken shits in

00:37:24.990 --> 00:37:26.430
each one of their toilets and just

00:37:26.430 --> 00:37:28.750
left it there. Again, this nice message

00:37:28.750 --> 00:37:31.110
from the Mossad, we know who you are.

00:37:31.870 --> 00:37:33.590
There's nothing you can do to stop us.

00:37:34.550 --> 00:37:36.030
Finally, at the end of their two-year

00:37:36.030 --> 00:37:39.430
tour, they go to a going away party that

00:37:39.430 --> 00:37:40.990
the ambassador had for them. They go back

00:37:40.990 --> 00:37:42.710
to their house. Somebody had cut the

00:37:42.710 --> 00:37:45.430
dog's tail off and then wrapped it in

00:37:45.430 --> 00:37:48.710
gauze and medical tape. Like, why would

00:37:48.710 --> 00:37:51.230
you do something like that? Why harass

00:37:51.230 --> 00:37:54.230
this couple that is doing literally

00:37:54.230 --> 00:37:57.670
nothing to you, that is known to you,

00:37:57.870 --> 00:37:59.550
has been declared to you. Why would

00:37:59.550 --> 00:38:01.630
you fuck with them like that? But

00:38:01.670 --> 00:38:04.030
this is what the Israelis do. That's

00:38:04.030 --> 00:38:04.510
how they work.

00:38:05.550 --> 00:38:07.270
Yeah, I mean, it seems like they have

00:38:07.270 --> 00:38:11.670
a cultural obsession with dominance,

00:38:12.030 --> 00:38:12.710
obviously.

00:38:16.030 --> 00:38:19.190
And so, yeah, even a couple of my

00:38:19.190 --> 00:38:22.630
friends were foreign area officers in

00:38:22.630 --> 00:38:24.870
the military throughout West Asia.

00:38:25.190 --> 00:38:26.750
And one of the classes you go

00:38:26.750 --> 00:38:27.870
through, it's like, who does the

00:38:27.870 --> 00:38:29.950
most, around globally, who does the

00:38:29.950 --> 00:38:32.390
most adversarial collection on US

00:38:32.390 --> 00:38:34.590
military officers? It's not Russia.

00:38:34.950 --> 00:38:36.670
No, it's not China. Yeah.

00:38:37.190 --> 00:38:40.750
No. Israel was right, was raided at

00:38:40.750 --> 00:38:42.750
the CIA as critical threat for

00:38:42.750 --> 00:38:45.270
counterintelligence. So it was it

00:38:45.270 --> 00:38:48.150
was Israel, Russia, China, Cuba and

00:38:48.150 --> 00:38:50.510
Iran and North Korea. Those were the

00:38:50.510 --> 00:38:54.190
critical threat countries. Yeah, it's

00:38:54.190 --> 00:38:55.590
bad, really bad.

00:38:56.430 --> 00:38:59.430
Yeah. And of course, the disconnect

00:38:59.430 --> 00:39:01.550
between the intelligence services and

00:39:01.550 --> 00:39:04.790
the politicians who give a political

00:39:04.790 --> 00:39:07.270
talking point must be very grating to

00:39:07.270 --> 00:39:08.550
the people who serve in those

00:39:08.550 --> 00:39:10.790
institutions. And the funny thing too

00:39:10.790 --> 00:39:12.910
is, you know, at the State Department

00:39:12.910 --> 00:39:14.350
among foreign service officers, it's

00:39:14.350 --> 00:39:17.310
no secret what the Israelis do.

00:39:17.310 --> 00:39:19.070
There was no love of the Israelis

00:39:19.230 --> 00:39:20.550
inside the State Department. But

00:39:20.550 --> 00:39:22.270
you're right, the pressure comes

00:39:22.270 --> 00:39:23.910
from the policy community, comes from

00:39:23.910 --> 00:39:26.190
Capitol Hill, from the White House

00:39:26.190 --> 00:39:28.390
and Capitol Hill at the State

00:39:28.390 --> 00:39:30.550
Department, and especially at the CIA,

00:39:30.790 --> 00:39:33.190
you don't need to take those political

00:39:33.470 --> 00:39:36.830
issues into consideration. But you

00:39:38.310 --> 00:39:40.870
you have to carry out the foreign

00:39:40.870 --> 00:39:43.590
policy of the United States, whether

00:39:43.590 --> 00:39:44.390
you like it or not.

00:39:45.510 --> 00:39:48.630
Yeah, it just reminds me just kind of

00:39:48.630 --> 00:39:51.110
like wrap this up when I first started

00:39:51.110 --> 00:39:54.510
like branching more into like an

00:39:54.510 --> 00:39:56.870
intelligence role within my unit,

00:39:57.310 --> 00:39:58.790
kind of like my mentor was like, you

00:39:58.790 --> 00:40:00.630
know what, despite what they're saying

00:40:00.630 --> 00:40:02.070
in Washington or anything like this,

00:40:02.070 --> 00:40:04.510
if we pull out, the entire government

00:40:04.510 --> 00:40:05.790
will collapse in two weeks. And that

00:40:05.790 --> 00:40:08.750
was in 2011. And nothing changed.

00:40:08.750 --> 00:40:10.110
But again, I guess we're just going

00:40:10.110 --> 00:40:12.270
to keep putting money and resources

00:40:12.270 --> 00:40:14.630
into it. So yeah, that was also a

00:40:14.630 --> 00:40:16.070
very frustrating foreign policy. But

00:40:16.070 --> 00:40:18.590
anyways, thank you so much for

00:40:18.590 --> 00:40:20.350
coming on. And you got a heart out.

00:40:20.390 --> 00:40:23.910
Yeah. So John Kiriakou, yeah, he's

00:40:24.390 --> 00:40:27.670
he's got a new series on a Unify TV

00:40:27.670 --> 00:40:29.350
dot com link in descriptions. And

00:40:29.350 --> 00:40:30.950
also he's written a number of books

00:40:31.230 --> 00:40:35.230
on CIA whistleblowing, etc. Really

00:40:35.230 --> 00:40:37.110
appreciate your time. And my

00:40:37.110 --> 00:40:38.390
pleasure. Thanks for having me.

00:40:39.270 --> 00:40:41.390
All right. And thank you all for

00:40:41.390 --> 00:40:44.630
watching. We will be back next

00:40:44.670 --> 00:40:47.030
week. Cheers, y'all. Have a good

00:40:47.030 --> 00:40:47.430
weekend.

